public class Example {
    public void doSomething(@NonNull String param) {
        if (param == null) {
            throw new NullPointerException("param is marked non-null but is null");
        }
        System.out.println(param);
    }
}
```
As you can see, Lombok has generated code that checks if the `param` parameter is null before executing the method body. If `param` is null, Lombok throws a `NullPointerException` with a message that indicates which parameter was null.

