```
let array = [1, 2, 2, 3, 3, 3, 4, 4, 4, 4];
let seen = new Set();
array = array.filter(value => {
    if (seen.has(value)) {
        return false;
    }
    seen.add(value);
    return true;
});
// array is now [1, 2, 3, 4]
```
1. Using the `reduce()` method and a callback function that adds unique values to an object:
```
let array = [1, 2, 2, 3, 3, 3, 4, 4, 4, 4];
array = array.reduce((acc, value) => {
    if (!acc[value]) {
        acc[value] = true;
        return acc;
    }
    return acc;
}, {});
array = Object.keys(array);
// array is now [1, 2, 3, 4]
```
